Package: sequnit
Type: Package
Title: Sequential Monitoring of Randomised Unit Tests
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Efthymios", "Costa", email = "efthymios.costa17@imperial.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Axel", "Gandy", role = "aut"))
Description: Monitors randomised unit tests across successive code changes
    with a non-restarting cumulative sum (CUSUM) chart. Each test supplies a
    p-value, and the chart accumulates evidence of a code defect. The chart is
    optimised to minimise the average number of user commits until a signal
    when a defect is present, while ensuring a desired average number of user commits
    and a fixed computational budget when no code defects are present.
    The package designs the chart, records its state in JSON Lines logs,
    offers functions for plotting the logs, and provides a
    GitHub Actions workflow template for developers to use for sequential testing
    of non-deterministic tests.
